    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nI've had a look and haven't found a way to cause mini.clue to show clues for the top level binds, i.e. before hitting any key. \r\nWhen using which-key, I had a bind of `<leader><leader>` mapped to `<cmd>WhichKey<cr>` which achieved this result, so my request is just to have something similar, either a command or a lua method to bring up a list of any clues for top level binds, as well as all defined mini.clue triggers.",
