    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nYou can see all the triggers by inspecting `MiniClue.config.triggers` and `vim.b.miniclue_config` (if present). There is also a more dynamic way to inspect the output of `vim.api.nvim_buf_get_keymap(0, 'n')`.\r\n\r\nI don't really see a big advantage of having a separate method to show all triggers interactively in a clue window.\r\n\r\nThere also was an attempt to create a function that starts a query without triggers: #442. It was met with a lot of tricky issues and was deemed not worth the time and effort.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
